<title>SWEDEN: SWIMMING-WORLD SHORT-COURSE CHAMPIONSHIPS MEDALS TABLE.</title>
<headline>SWIMMING-WORLD SHORT-COURSE CHAMPIONSHIPS MEDALS TABLE.</headline>
<dateline>GOTHENBURG, Sweden 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Medals table at the</p>
<p>end of the second day of the four-day world short-course</p>
<p>swimming championsips:</p>
<p>		   Gold    Silver    Bronze</p>
<p> Australia	 6	  1	   3</p>
<p> China	     3	  4	   2</p>
<p> Sweden	    2	  2	   -</p>
<p> Germany	   1	  3	   3</p>
<p> United States   1	  2	   3</p>
<p> Brazil	    1	  -	   -</p>
<p> Costa Rica	1	  -	   -</p>
<p> Cuba		1	  -	   -</p>
<p> Denmark	   1	  -	   -</p>
<p> Russia	    -	  2	   1</p>
<p> Japan	     -	  1	   -</p>
<p> New Zealand     -	  1	   -</p>
<p> Romania	   -	  1	   -</p>
<p> Britain	   -	  -	   2</p>
<p> Canada	    -	  -	   1</p>
<p> Netherlands     -	  -	   1</p>
<p> Poland	    -	  -	   1</p>
<p> Slovakia	  -	  -	   1</p>
<p>Note: two bronze medals were awarded in the men's 400 metres</p>
<p>individual medley.</p>
</text>
